Description: AHCI interrupt ordering fix for Marvell 88SE61xx (DKMS)
 Rebuilds the ahci kernel module with a fix for Marvell 88SE6111/6121/6145
 SATA controllers, which stop reporting interrupts for a port when
 HOST_IRQ_STAT is cleared while PxIS still holds bits.  The completion of the
 command in flight is then lost and the command only ends in a timeout, so
 SATA-2 and SATA-3 disks fail to be identified at all.
 .
 The fix gives these controllers a private interrupt handler that clears the
 host status before servicing the ports, which is what Marvell's own driver for
 this chip family does.
 .
 The module sources are not shipped: they are extracted from Debian's own
 linux-source package at build time, so the private header drivers/ata/ahci.h
 matches the one the distribution's libahci.ko was built against.
 .
 See https://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=216094
